// GenerativeUiInterfaceShowSurfaceMessage Show a UI on the device's screen and bring the Port OS app to the foreground. It replaces any surface already on screen (a device shows one surface at a time) and starts a new sequence for the surface at 1.
//
// How to use this interface: call get-components first to learn the components and the screen (960 by 540 dp on a TV, ten-foot viewing distance: use large text and few items). Send show-surface with the whole first UI, then small update-surface calls to change it in place, then close-surface. Confirm what is on screen with get-surface.
//
// Shape: `surfaceId` names the surface; `a2ui` is a list of A2UI v1.0 server-to-client messages for that surface. Include a `createSurface` message and a component with the id `root`. Components are a flat list; containers name their children by id. Every message must target `surfaceId` and use only supported components and properties, otherwise the call is refused with BAD_REQUEST naming the component or property. Minimal example:
//
// ```json
// {"surfaceId": "hello", "a2ui": [
//
//	{"version": "1.0", "createSurface": {"surfaceId": "hello", "catalogId": "https://a2ui.org/specification/v1_0/catalogs/basic/catalog.json",
//	  "components": [
//	    {"id": "root", "component": "Column", "children": ["title", "body"]},
//	    {"id": "title", "component": "Text", "text": "# Dinner at 7"},
//	    {"id": "body", "component": "Text", "text": "Pasta is almost ready."}]}}]}
//
// ```
//
